      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Barnes's mother sued Felix on Barnes's behalf, alleging that Felix violated Barnes's Fourth Amendment right against excessive force."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lanora C. Pettit",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Lanora C. Pettit, Principal Deputy Solicitor General of Texas, argued the cause for Texas et al. as amici curiae supporting respondent Felix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We reject that approach as improperly narrowing the requisite Fourth Amendment analysis. To assess whether an offcer acted reasonably in using force, a court must consider all the rele- vant circumstances, including facts and events leading up to the climactic moment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And because that was the reasoning in the case before us,\nthat is the reasoning we must address. It could make no\ndifference to our decision here if the Fifth Circuit in other\ncases eschewed a strict time limit, as Felix claims. And\nanyway, we are not sure Felix correctly describes the overall\nstate of Fifth Circuit law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Likewise, serial killer Ted Bundy was pulled over based on a stolen-vehicle alert in Pensacola, Florida."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Scott v. Harris, multiple police cars \u201cwith blue lights fashing and sirens blaring\u201d chased the driver \u201cfor nearly 10 miles\u201d while \u201che ignored their warning to stop,\u201d culminating in an offcer ramming the driver off the road."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even if the offcer manages to hit the tires, the driver could lose control and crash into others on the road."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2454ec25332d9fc45e9e38c0b0af24881f604092c21d3574adcd338e35f255d1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2454ec25332d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\u201csplit-second judgments\u201d on the ground, \u201cin circumstances that are tense, uncertain, and rapidly evolving.\u201d Id., at 397."
    }
  ],
